WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:08.000
<v Priya Shah>Morning everyone, it's the 10:30 huddle. Quick round on blockers and anything for the RAID log.</v>

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:17.000
<v Aisha Khan>Good news on ERP. The vendor fixed the sandbox endpoints yesterday and the read-only calls have been stable for two days.</v>

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:26.000
<v Aisha Khan>So I think we can close the sandbox issue. We're still behind on the build itself, but the sandbox is no longer the blocker.</v>

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.000
<v Priya Shah>Great, close it. Ben, where are we on cleansing?</v>

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:40.000
<v Ben Carter>Still at around eighteen percent duplicates. The two extra SMEs start on Monday, and Sales Ops signed off the dedupe rules on Wednesday.</v>

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:47.000
<v Ben Carter>If the dedupe run on Thursday doesn't get us under ten percent, the trial migration will slip again.</v>

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:56.000
<v Grace Kim>One new one from me. We haven't booked the performance test environment yet, and the platform team says it's three weeks' lead time.</v>

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:06.000
<v Grace Kim>There's a real risk the performance environment won't be ready before performance testing starts on the thirtieth of November. I'll own that one.</v>

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:15.000
<v Priya Shah>Okay, log it as a risk, Grace as owner, probably medium likelihood but high impact. Grace, can you raise the booking request today?</v>

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.000
<v Grace Kim>Yes, I will raise the booking request today.</v>

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:25.000
<v Priya Shah>On UAT testers, I'll confirm the UAT slots with Sales leadership by Friday the sixth.</v>

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:34.000
<v Marcus Lee>Also, someone needs to chase the identity team about the SSO configuration, it was due on the twentieth and nobody has heard back.</v>

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:38.000
<v Priya Shah>Noted, let's get that chased.</v>

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:42.000
<v Aisha Khan>And for the record on the API freeze, are we agreed?</v>

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:50.000
<v Priya Shah>Yes. So we're agreed: no ERP API changes from the first of December until after go-live. I'll tell the vendor.</v>

00:01:51.000 --> 00:02:00.000
<v Marcus Lee>Marketing Ops told me the marketing automation sandbox will be ready on the twentieth of November, so that dependency is in progress now.</v>

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:04.000
<v Priya Shah>Thanks all. That's it for today.</v>
